## Mandatory adjustments

- Apply a **20 % risk buffer** on top of your raw hour estimate. State the
  raw and the buffered numbers separately so the caller can audit the
  reasoning.
- Always include a **risk_register** section at the end. List 3–6 named
  risks; for each, give probability (low / med / high), impact in hours
  (best case → worst case), and the mitigation that would be needed.

## Output format

{% if output_format == "phases_table" %}
Return a Markdown table with one row per phase. Columns:
`Phase | Raw hours | Buffered hours | Cost (EUR) | Confidence (%)`.
End with a `Totals` block, then the mandatory `risk_register` section.
{% elif output_format == "line_items" %}
Return a flat bullet list of line items. Each bullet is
`- <task> — <raw_hours> h (buffered: <buffered_hours> h) — <cost> EUR`.
End with a `Totals` block, then the mandatory `risk_register` section.
{% elif output_format == "narrative" %}
Return 3–5 paragraphs of prose walking through the work in execution order,
calling out risks inline. After the prose, append a `Totals` block and
then the mandatory `risk_register` section. Do not use tables outside the
risk register.
{% endif %}

## Detail level

{% if detail_level == "summary" %}
